.claude/plans/PLAN-161/pair-rail/w2-round-2.md:13:3. F12 [P1] .claude/workflows/council-audit.js:248: Removing `ARTIFACT_KEEP_DIR` did not close the artifact-path redirect class. `mktemp -d -t` honors inherited `TMPDIR`; if it points inside the repo, the lane writes there and the stale sweep at line 250 recursively deletes matching directories there, contradicting read-only containment and “never the repo tree.”
.claude/plans/PLAN-161/pair-rail/w2-round-2.md:15:4. F13 [P2] .claude/workflows/council-audit.js:328: The attestation gate identifies Grok by `REQUESTED_VENDORS[i]` but returns the original model-written lane object. Downstream attribution still trusts `l.vendor` at line 354, allowing a lane to impersonate another vendor and corrupt availability, finding attribution, disagreements, audit instructions, and the attestation map.
