The tag-liveness cure itself is sound: one remote advertisement is parsed for both peeled and plain refs; deleted/moved tags fail closed; signed annotated tags compare their peeled commit to the same commit identity already enforced by `HEAD == GITHUB_SHA`; lightweight tags fall back to the plain ref; and the already-published no-op remains green. I did, however, find two release-ceremony integration failures outside that guard.
